<code>assert \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size())-1; (this.get(i) == null) => (this.get(i+1) == \old(this.get(i))) || (this.get(i+1) == \old(this.get(i+1)));</code>

However, the above assertion seems to be more complex than necessary based on the comment. The comment suggests that after adding an element at a specific index, all elements from that index to the old size minus one should shift right by one position. Therefore, a simpler and more accurate assertion would be:

<code>assert \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); this.get(i+1) == \old(this.get(i));</code>

This assertion states that for every index `i` from the given `index` to the old size minus one, the element at position `i+1` after the addition is equal to the element at position `i` before the addition.
--------------------
<code>assert \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size())-1; (this.get(i) == null) => (this.get(i+1) == \old(this.get(i))) || (this.get(i+1) == \old(this.get(i+1)));</code>

This assertion ensures that for every element from the given index to the old size minus one, if the current element is null, the next element should also be null, otherwise, the next element should remain unchanged.
--------------------
<code>assert \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size())-1; (this.get(i) == null) => (this.get(i+1) == \old(this.get(i))) || (this.get(i+1) == \old(this.get(i+1)));</code>

However, the condition seems to be more naturally expressed as ensuring that each element from the new index to the old size minus one is shifted correctly. Here's a refined version:

<code>assert \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i-1));</code>

This captures the essence that each element from the insertion point to the end of the list is shifted by one position to the right.
